namespace pdg { /**

\fn boolean pdg::FileManager::findNext(FileFindData ioFindData)

\brief advance a file/directory search and update its search object

Continue the search using the same object returned by findFirst(). This updates
that object's nodeName, isDirectory, and found fields in place. When the return
value is true, nodeName and isDirectory describe the next matching item. When
it is false, the search is exhausted and found is false; do not use the other
fields as a new result. Call findClose() with this same object to release the
search resources.

\param ioFindData the original object returned by findFirst(), updated in place
\return true if another matching item was found, otherwise false

\sa findFirst
\sa findClose

**/ }
